  "details": "I regularly have to login on Quest, which is a pain, and not something I ever had to do in any other game that I played. Logging in using the henpeck system is a serious pain. In the 21st century, that is something you should have to do only once on each device. And if that wasn't already user-hostile enough, despite having 2FA disabled, VRChat still sometimes sends me a login code. If that happens, I have to walk to another room, go to my computer, check my E-Mail, walk back to the room where I play VRChat on my quest, and hope the login window is still there and has not slipped into a wall or something. And then I have to hope I remembered the code correctly. So please, make it so that you only have to log in a single time on quest. And also please don't require an E-Mail code on Quest unless users explicitly opt in on that feature. To me it's torture! So please let me at least opt out.",
